{"id": "EUVD-2026-103807", "enisaUuid": "8c2b6c46-944d-3359-9d84-7f6082c288a0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-pcache: bound the logical key offset from persistent memory\n\ncache_key_decode() takes a key's logical off from the cache device and\nlater indexes req_key_tree->subtrees[] by it in get_subtree(). An off\npast the device forms a subtree pointer outside the array, which\nrb_insert() writes through during replay.\n\nReject a key of zero length, or whose off+len (computed in 64 bits)\nexceeds the device size, before it is used.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:51:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:27:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d5a87cb909c1f375f08065b20123fa5db5958d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/10449703200076980704894c3d68d6796182371b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97fc4b53dbe4a983fdf093243067fa6a64562307"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f472-jf6w-c35h", "CVE-2026-98867"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "335dd1c9-ae0e-31ea-a162-95b0c7decaa3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <3d5a87cb909c1f375f08065b20123fa5db5958d8"}, {"id": "4232a73c-ec2d-39cf-94aa-e9b554137230", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <10449703200076980704894c3d68d6796182371b"}, {"id": "5474dfdf-bcc9-37f9-aad4-57ec682096fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6b51ab1b-e0f8-3aea-a8bb-81614844e442", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <97fc4b53dbe4a983fdf093243067fa6a64562307"}, {"id": "79267292-9bcf-37b5-af0a-2a6670fcaf97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "876a402b-b933-33cd-9792-a